n  neighborhoods around kiev  the capital observing a 35-hour curfew  to prepare for an expected russian  assault  today is a special and dangerous moment  movement through the city is prohibited  without special passes you can only go  out to reach a shelter the curfew will  apply until 7 am on march 17th therefore  i ask all kiev residents to prepare for  the fact that they will have to be at  home for two days or in case of an alarm  in a shelter  diplomacy remains the only way to end  this war says ukraine's leader  it is important it is difficult but  important because any war ends in an  agreement meetings continue as i am told  the positions in the negotiations sound  more realistic however there still needs  to be more time for decisions to be in  ukraine's interests  the west of the country has avoided the  worst of the violence but the largest  single missile attack so far happened at  a military training camp in yavariv only  about an hour's drive away from here  residents say that unless there is a  ceasefire it's not a matter of if but  when the fighting makes its way here  zain basravi al-jazeera level
 

